CRASH-11: clear the segment pool pointer when closing quality

closequal() deletes the water quality segment pool but leaves
qual->SegPool pointing at the freed pool. EN_closeQ does not check
whether the solver is open, so a second call, such as EN_closeQ after
EN_solveQ, deletes the pool again. Set the pointer to NULL after the
delete, as the FREE() calls next to it already do for the other arrays.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply CRASH-11_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/quality.c b/src/quality.c
index 36c89b9..b340dda 100644
--- a/src/quality.c
+++ b/src/quality.c
@@ -406,6 +406,7 @@ int closequal(Project *pr)
     if (qual->Qualflag != NONE)
     {
         if (qual->SegPool) mempool_delete(qual->SegPool);
+        qual->SegPool = NULL;
         FREE(qual->FirstSeg);
         FREE(qual->LastSeg);
         FREE(qual->PipeRateCoeff);
